-- #1111 A-2.6: an IMPORT-vs-IMPORT ordering guard.
--
-- Two imports, in this order: `hja.{HA}` names only the TYPE `HA`; `hjz.{HZ, Hit,
-- unHZ}` names the CONSTRUCTOR `Hit`.  The overlay is registered in SOURCE ORDER and
-- is last-wins within itself, so if `hja` contributed a decl it would land BEFORE
-- `hjz`'s and lose — but if the two clauses were swapped, or if `hja` matched by a
-- route this one does not, `HA`'s `Hit : Int -> HA` would out-rank the `Hit` this
-- file actually imports and `Hit "s"` would be rejected.
--
-- Expected output, derived by hand: `s`.  `Hit` is imported by name from `hjz` only,
-- so `Hit "s" : HZ` and `unHZ v` is `"s"`.
--
-- ⚠️ WHY `hja.{HA}` CONTRIBUTES NOTHING HERE — state it precisely, because the
-- general claim is FALSE.  Rule (b) of `importedCtorTypeDecls` is a CONSTRUCTOR-name
-- test: `HA` contributes nothing because no decl of `hja` has a constructor spelled
-- `HA` (its one variant is `Hit`), NOT because members that look like type names are
-- inert.  Give `hja` a `data Wrapper = HA Int` and the member matches by rule (b) —
-- `test/llvm_fixtures_modules/ctor_scope_type_only_sibling_decl/` is that shape,
-- measured.  An earlier revision of this header asserted the general property and an
-- unrun counterfactual for it; both are withdrawn rather than re-pointed.
--
-- ⚠️ HONEST SCOPE: this fixture is GREEN on pristine `main` too (verified first-hand
-- on a binary built from 40756bea: `check` exit 0, `run` prints `s`) — main has no
-- overlay for this member either.  It pins a PRESERVED property, not a repaired one,
-- and it is NOT an over-registration detector: for those, see
-- `ctor_scope_local_decl_wins/`, `ctor_scope_type_only_sibling_decl/` and
-- `test/engine_fixtures/ctor_scope_local_ctor_beats_stdlib_import.mdk`, each of which
-- goes RED when the overlay out-ranks something it should not.
import hja.{HA}
import hjz.{HZ, Hit, unHZ}

v : HZ
v = Hit "s"

main : <IO> Unit
main = putStrLn (unHZ v)
